diff --git a/docs/ai/contracts/B04-checkout.md b/docs/ai/contracts/B04-checkout.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..186de25
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ai/contracts/B04-checkout.md
@@ -0,0 +1,144 @@
+# Contract: B04 — Cart & Checkout (discounts, shipping, address, safe order placement)
+
+Owner: B04. Depends on: B05 (`OrderService.createPendingOrder`, `PENDING_PAYMENT`), B03 (`InventoryGateway.reserve`,
+`InventoryService.availableFor`; lock-ordering rule, contract B03 section 4), B08 (`AddressService.getOwned`), B01-F1 (`/api/v1`
+envelope, `ApiPaging`), B01-P3 (`discount:view`, `discount:manage`). Migrations: `V40`, `V41` (hand-applied).
+
+## 1. Cart — `/api/v1/cart` (any logged-in user; the cart is always the token user's)
+
+| Method | Path | Body | Result |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| GET | `/` | — | 200 the cart |
+| POST | `/items` | `{ productId, quantity? }` (default 1, 1..1000) | 200 the whole cart |
+| PATCH | `/items/{id}` | `{ quantity }` (1..1000, the new absolute quantity) | 200 the whole cart |
+| DELETE | `/items/{id}` | — | 200 the whole cart |
+| DELETE | `/` | — | 204 (empties the cart) |
+
+Cart shape: `{ cartId, items: [{ id, product (ProductResponse), quantity, subtotal, availableQuantity, warning }], totalPrice, totalItems }`.
+`availableQuantity` is on hand minus reserved (same number as `product.stockQuantity`). `warning` is a customer-facing sentence
+written by the server (`null` when the line is fine): `Sản phẩm "X" hiện không còn kinh doanh.` / `… đã hết hàng.` /
+`… chỉ còn N sản phẩm trong kho.`; the cart page shows it as it is. `totalPrice` is the sum of price x quantity and is **not** the
+amount to pay (shipping and discounts are added at checkout).
+
+Rules: adding or raising a quantity beyond what is available → 400 `Kho chỉ còn N sản phẩm.`; a withdrawn (not `ACTIVE`) product cannot be added.
+**Ownership** is part of the item query (`ci.id = :id AND ci.cart.user.id = :tokenUserId`), so another user's item looks exactly like a
+missing one (404) and ids cannot be probed. Bodies are typed records; unknown JSON fields are ignored. `PUT /items/{id}` no longer exists.
+
+## 2. Checkout — `/api/v1/checkout` (any logged-in user)
+
+### `CheckoutRequest` (both endpoints)
+
+```json
+{ "addressId": 7,                                   // a saved address of the caller (B08) ... 
+  "customerName": "An", "customerPhone": "0900000000", "shippingAddress": "1 Lê Lợi, ...",   // ... OR these three text fields
+  "discountCode": "SALE10",                         // optional, any case
+  "paymentMethod": "COD" }                          // COD | VIETQR | MOMO (case-insensitive); required by POST /checkout
+```
+
+When `addressId` is present the text fields are ignored; the address must belong to the caller (403 `FORBIDDEN` otherwise, 404 if it does
+not exist). Without `addressId` all three text fields are required (400). Either way the data is **copied** into the order
+(`customer_name`, `customer_phone`, `shipping_address` = `line1, ward, district, province` for a saved address): an order never references
+the address book, so editing or deleting an address cannot change an order. The record has no field for a price, total, discount amount,
+shipping, status or user id, so none can be sent; extra JSON properties are ignored; the customer is the token user.
+
+### `POST /api/v1/checkout` → 201 `{ data: OrderResponse }`
+
+`OrderResponse` is the B05 shape (`id`, `status` = `PENDING_PAYMENT`, `subtotal`, `discountAmount`, `shippingFee`, `totalPrice`,
+`discountCode`, snapshot fields, `items`). Errors (`{error:{code,message}}`): empty cart or inactive product or bad discount code → 400
+`BUSINESS_RULE_VIOLATION`; not enough stock → 400 `BUSINESS_RULE_VIOLATION` whose message names the product; unknown payment method or missing
+recipient text → 400 `BAD_REQUEST`/`VALIDATION_ERROR`; foreign `addressId` → 403.
+
+### `POST /api/v1/checkout/preview` → 200 `{ data: CheckoutPreview }`  (no side effect)
+
+```json
+{ "items": [{ "productId": 10, "name": "Bình nước", "unitPrice": 100000, "quantity": 2, "lineTotal": 200000.00, "available": 5 }],
+  "subtotal": 200000.00, "discountAmount": 0.00, "shippingFee": 30000.00, "total": 230000.00,
+  "discountCode": null,                                   // the stored (upper-case) code when it was accepted
+  "issues": [{ "productId": null, "code": "DISCOUNT_INVALID", "message": "Mã giảm giá không hợp lệ hoặc đã hết hạn." }] }
+```
+The body may be empty or `{discountCode}`; address and payment method are not needed. The preview takes **no lock and writes nothing**
+(no reservation, no order, no cart change, no event); problems are reported in `issues` (`CART_EMPTY`, `PRODUCT_UNAVAILABLE`, `OUT_OF_STOCK`,
+`INSUFFICIENT_STOCK`, `DISCOUNT_INVALID`; `productId` is null for cart-level issues) and the numbers are still returned. It uses the same pricing
+code as checkout, so a preview and the checkout that follows agree unless the cart, stock or code changed in between. A withdrawn product
+is listed but not charged; a rejected code takes nothing off.
+
+## 3. `CheckoutService.checkout(userId, request)` — one `@Transactional`, in this order
+
+0. Pure request checks (payment method known) — before anything is read or locked.
+1. **Lock the cart row**: `CartRepository.findByUserIdForUpdate(userId)` = `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` (`PESSIMISTIC_WRITE`, JPA lock-timeout hint
+   3000 ms; whether the PostgreSQL dialect honours the hint is not verified). A second concurrent checkout of the same cart waits here, then reads the
+   already emptied cart → 400 "Giỏ hàng của bạn đang trống." **One cart produces one order.** No cart row = empty cart (400).
+2. Items **with** products (and categories) in ONE query (`findByCartIdWithProduct`); no items → 400.
+3. Per item: product `ACTIVE`, quantity > 0, enough stock (ONE batched `InventoryService.availableFor`; `InventoryGateway` has no batch method and the B03 interface
+   is unchanged). A price comes from the product row just loaded, never from the cart or the client.
+4. `subtotal = Σ price × quantity`.
+5. Discount code (if any): see section 4.
+6. `shippingFee`: see section 5.
+7. `total = subtotal − discount + shipping`, `BigDecimal` scale 2.
+8. Recipient snapshot (section 2), then `orderService.createPendingOrder(...)` (B05; it re-validates `total = subtotal − discount + shipping`).
+9. `InventoryGateway.reserve(productId, quantity, "ORDER", orderId)` per item in **ascending productId** (B03 lock-ordering rule). An
+   `InsufficientStockException` anywhere rolls back everything, including the order row.
+10. `PaymentService.createPendingPayment(order, method)` — `Payment(PENDING)`, amount = the order total, no gateway.
+11. Delete the cart items **last** (the final write).
+Then (read-only) load the order items for the response and publish `OrderPlacedEvent`. Any exception after step 1 rolls back the order, the
+reservations, the payment and the cart clearing together, and the cart stays as it was.
+
+## 4. Discounts
+
+Table `discounts` (V40): `code` (stored UPPER-CASE, unique on `upper(code)`), `percent_off` (1..100) **xor** `amount_off` (> 0, VND), optional
+`min_order_amount`, `valid_from`, `valid_to`, `active`, `created_at`. A code is usable when it exists, is `active`, `valid_from <= now <= valid_to` (open ends
+allowed, bounds inclusive) and `subtotal >= min_order_amount` (equal is accepted). Percent discounts are rounded to **whole VND, `HALF_UP`**
+(15 % of 99 990 = 14 998.5 → 14 999). The discount never exceeds the subtotal (a larger fixed amount or 100 % takes off exactly the subtotal).
+Matching is case-insensitive. **Every** failure — unknown, inactive, not yet valid, expired, below the minimum — answers with the same message
+`Mã giảm giá không hợp lệ hoặc đã hết hạn.` (no enumeration hint). No discount state is stored in the cart (the code is sent at preview/checkout). The order stores the
+code text and the amount applied; there is no foreign key, so deleting or editing a code never changes an old order.
+
+Admin API `/api/v1/admin/discounts` (no admin UI here; B12): `GET /` (paged: `page`, `size` ≤ 100, `sort` ∈ `id`, `code`, `createdAt`, `validTo`; filters `keyword`, `active`), `GET /{id}` need
+`discount:view`; `POST /` (201), `PUT /{id}`, `DELETE /{id}` (204) need `discount:manage`. Body `{ code (3-30, letters, digits, - _), percentOff | amountOff (exactly one),
+minOrderAmount?, validFrom?, validTo?, active? (default true) }`. Duplicate code (any case) → 409 `CONFLICT`; both or neither of percent/amount, or `validFrom > validTo` → 400;
+unknown id → 404. `discount:view` does not imply `discount:manage` (and the reverse). V41 grants both to ADMIN and MANAGER (decision D-6); CUSTOMER gets none.
+
+## 5. Shipping (owner decision D-10)
+
+Configuration (`application.properties`, override by environment): `ecogreen.shipping.flat-fee` = `${SHIPPING_FLAT_FEE:30000}` and
+`ecogreen.shipping.free-threshold` = `${FREE_SHIPPING_THRESHOLD:500000}`, in VND, both must be `>= 0` (the application refuses to start otherwise).
+**The fee is charged unless the goods amount after discount (`subtotal − discount`) is at least the threshold; exactly the threshold is free.** The
+amount after discount is compared (a coupon that drops the goods below the threshold brings the fee back). An empty cart has no shipping. This rule
+was not written in the spec (it only names the two properties); it is recorded here as the chosen behaviour.
+
+**Customer-visible change:** until now no shipping was charged; from this release an order below 500 000 ₫ costs 30 000 ₫ more. Orders placed before keep
+the totals stored on them. The cart page no longer says "Miễn phí" and shows only the subtotal; the checkout page shows the server's breakdown.
+
+## 6. Event
+
+`OrderPlacedEvent(Long orderId, Long userId, BigDecimal total)` (package `event`) is published by `CheckoutService` inside the checkout transaction. Consumers
+(B09 notifications, B10 analytics) must use `@TransactionalEventListener(phase = AFTER_COMMIT)`: they then receive it only for an order that was really committed, and never for a
+rolled-back checkout (`OrderPlacedEventAfterCommitTest` shows this with real transaction synchronisation).
+
+## 7. Removed legacy
+
+`POST /api/orders` (`OrderController`), `/api/cart/*` (`CartController`), `OrderService.checkout` and `OrderService.getItems`, and the unused cart repositories
+fields of `OrderService`. The frontend (`cartApi.js`, `orderApi.js`, `CartContext.jsx`, `Cart.jsx`, `Checkout.jsx`) was migrated in the same change.
+`CartService.getOrCreateCart(User)` and `createCartForUser(User)` keep their signatures because B01 `AuthService` calls them.
+
+## 8. TEMPORARY-COMPAT
+
+| Where | What | Remove when |
+|---|---|---|
+| `PaymentService.createPendingPayment` (+ `normalizeMethod`) | the minimal first payment row, moved from the old checkout | B06 replaces the mock payment flow |
+
+Removed in B04: B05's legacy checkout (`OrderService.checkout`) and `OrderService.getItems`.
+
+## 9. Known limits
+
+* **Abandoned `PENDING_PAYMENT` orders keep their stock reserved forever** — there is no expiry job (out of scope; needs B06 or a scheduled task). Until then an unpaid
+  order must be cancelled by hand (cancelling releases the reservation).
+* `getOrCreateCart` of a user who has no cart yet can still race with itself (unique `user_id` violation → 500) when two first requests arrive together; accounts get their cart at registration/login, so this
+  is only reachable for very old accounts.
+* The cart lock timeout hint is requested but not verified against PostgreSQL.
+
+## Requests for contract changes
+
+* **B03 (owner B03):** add `Map<Long,Integer> availableFor(Collection<Long>)` to the `InventoryGateway` port. B04 and `CartService` currently call
+  `InventoryService.availableFor` directly because the interface has no batch read.
+* **B06 (owner B06):** replace `createPendingPayment` (TEMPORARY-COMPAT) when the real payment flow is built; the payment amount must keep coming from the order total.
